= Status quo bias =

== Overview ==
'''Status quo bias''' is a disproportionate preference for maintaining an existing state or previously selected option.

== Possible mechanisms ==
Observed status-quo preference can reflect loss aversion, switching costs, uncertainty, regret avoidance, implied endorsement, effort, or informational value. The behavioral effect is not a single mechanism.

== Normative caution ==
Remaining with the status quo can be rational when change has real costs. Bias claims require controlling those costs or specifying the normative benchmark.

== References ==
* William Samuelson & Richard Zeckhauser, “Status Quo Bias in Decision Making”, ''Journal of Risk and Uncertainty'' 1 (1988): 7–59.

